              is a non-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero-divisor"}> zero-divisor
              \.
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Given a commutative ring
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in R
              is a non-zero-divisor, then it is cancellative.
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Suppose that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in R
              is a non-zero-divisor. This means that for every element
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
